MINOR-5 — --scope safety check does not audit missing-from-scope files (reverse-BOB-068)
======================================================================

All three scenarios below ran the REAL, unmodified shipped
scripts/commit-push-all.sh end-to-end inside an isolated scratch git
sandbox with ZERO remotes configured (so stage 6's push loop is a safe
no-op — real script logic exercised, zero risk to the actual boba repo
or its upstreams).

Real reproduction: the declared --scope is a DIRECTORY that CONTAINS a
git SUBMODULE with uncommitted internal changes. 'git add <scope-dir>'
(stage 5's own staging call) stages the PARENT repo's tracked files
under that directory but does NOT reach INTO the submodule's own
working tree — the submodule's dirty content is a SEPARATE git-status
entity (the 'm'/'M' gitlink marker), genuinely left un-staged inside
the declared scope. This is directly relevant to the real boba repo,
which itself carries submodules/challenges + submodules/helixqa.

